---
title: "cancel (LegionPreLiquidOpenApplicationSale)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_check_auth: projectAdmin calls cancel()
    q_check_auth --> q_error_auth: caller is not projectAdmin
    q_error_auth --> [*]: revert Unauthorized
    q_check_auth --> q_check_supplied: caller is projectAdmin
    q_check_supplied --> q_error_supplied: tokensAlreadySupplied == true
    q_error_supplied --> [*]: revert TokensAlreadySupplied
    q_check_supplied --> q_check_cancelled: tokensAlreadySupplied == false
    q_check_cancelled --> q_error_cancelled: saleCancelled == true
    q_error_cancelled --> [*]: revert SaleAlreadyCancelled
    q_check_cancelled --> q_check_withdrawn: saleCancelled == false
    q_check_withdrawn --> q_require_return: capitalAlreadyWithdrawn == true
    q_check_withdrawn --> q_set_cancel: capitalAlreadyWithdrawn == false
    q_require_return --> q_check_returned: require project returns totalRaisedCapital + fees to contract
    q_check_returned --> q_error_insufficient: contract balance < totalRaisedCapital + fees
    q_error_insufficient --> [*]: revert InsufficientReturnedCapital
    q_check_returned --> q_set_cancel: contract balance >= totalRaisedCapital + fees
    q_set_cancel --> q_emit: saleCancelled = true
    q_emit --> [*]: emit SaleCancelled()

    note right of q_check_withdrawn
        INV-001: Cancellation only allowed before token supply
        INV-002: If capital was withdrawn, project must return full amount including fees
        INV-003: After cancellation, investors can withdraw via withdrawInvestedCapitalIfCanceled
        INV-004: saleCancelled transitions from false to true exactly once
    end note
